# Exact cached post-live --all findings; answers explain only the anchors of their class.

[step] This one-millimetre step is the 2.00 mm thick caption extension joining the 3.00 mm cut-face bearing and the 3.00 mm label pad. It lies below the unchanged neck's cut plane and keeps the recipe identifier reachable beyond the exposed source surface. It is not a layer-height or seam comparison edge.
alternatives: Making the extension uniformly 3.00 mm thick removes the step while adding stock below the caption; its lower face and handling/removal envelope need rechecking. A full rectangular bearing plate adds still more backing but fills the open passage view. Moving the label onto a larger separate tag adds another identity-bearing part.
