[ceiling] This Z 2.50 underside is the 3.00 mm thick cut-face bearing and caption assembly raised above the bed by its 2.50 mm storage key. Its shape retains the source cut ring; the hidden key has 0.25 mm side/bottom air in H. Automatic supports are retained for the holder and its open underside is reachable before assembly. The source neck's outer surface is not reshaped to make the holder self-supporting.
alternatives: A bed-facing bearing with a separately inserted larger key removes this ceiling but adds a joint and another part. Extending a solid base down around the key obstructs its mating storage cavity. A sloping bearing underside preserves the upper cut-ring datum but changes the underside section and requires a new storage/print-envelope review.
file: hardware/printed-parts/calibration/soda-studies/parts/n08d-neck-cut-face-foot.step
