[ceiling] These Z 5.50 underside faces belong to the existing-passage locator above the source cut-face plane. The locator is 1.80 mm high with 0.15 mm nominal passage air, held by the crossbar/stem so the unchanged neck withdraws on its 15-degree Y/Z passage axis. The holder uses automatic supports with the passage open from the bed side before assembly. The locator is a geometric seat, not a release-force qualification.
alternatives: A solid filled cut-face bearing backs more of the locator and reduces its underside support demand, but closes the passage view and adds material below the reference. A larger crossbar can back it locally but needs the passage-axis withdrawal and source-contact planes rechecked. A separate locator printed on its base adds alignment and attachment tolerances.
