alternatives: A larger crossbar or a completely filled cut-face disk removes these sharp boundary corners with more stock, but fills the open source-passage view and adds material below the sample. Rounded crossbar ends change the boundary and need source-bearing and locator access rechecked. Cutting off the corners removes cut-ring bearing area rather than enlarging it.
