alternatives: Filling this air backs the locator with more stock but changes the source passage seating/contact. A larger continuous bearing disk below the cut plane can enlarge its support without changing the source, but closes the passage view and adds material. Enlarging the passage air is another fit choice and does not thicken this boundary.
