[thin] These picks approach the hidden 6 by 8 mm storage key's top where it overlaps the cut-face bearing by 0.10 mm. They read the corner at Z 2.50–2.60; the key itself is 2.60 mm tall from the bed including this overlap. Exact representative midpoint occupancy confirms connected stock at this boundary, not a separate 0.370 or 0.395 mm roof. The insertion below the bearing is 2.50 mm.
alternatives: A larger full bearing disk closes the adjoining passage opening and increases backing at this corner. A deeper overlap grows the key into the bearing but changes the exposed key-top step within the opening. A separate long key adds another joint and increases the lift needed before individual sample withdrawal.
