[thin] These opposite surfaces bound the actual 1.20 mm internal T-head. Its underside projects 1.20 mm per X side beyond the 4.00 mm stem and receives the keeper's two lips. It is a small reference holder bearing, not a thin appliance wall or an accepted load-bearing joint; physical capture force and life remain unmeasured.
alternatives: A 2.40 or 3.00 mm head enlarges this section but needs a taller matching keeper slot/roof and renewed source-passage clearance. Increasing head width adds bearing area while requiring a wider slot and reducing neighboring keeper stock. A metal fastener changes the all-printed capture arrangement and adds another component.
