alternatives: A deeper 3.00 or 4.00 mm insertion adds engagement but increases the lift before radial exit and requires a new interference review with the next samples. A wider key increases stock but needs larger H sockets. A separate key can print the bearing on the bed but adds another attachment/alignment interface.
