[ledge] This horizontal underside is the internal T-head's retaining bearing, above the 4 by 4 mm stem. Its overhang is 1.20 mm per X side and 0.50 mm per Y side. The holder's prepared kit keeps automatic support decisions, with all sides reachable after the unchanged neck and keeper are removed. This is an accessible small capture bearing, not an inferred load/life result.
alternatives: A tapered underside removes the level bearing but changes the sliding keeper's retention/contact geometry. A thicker head preserves the bearing and requires a taller matching slot. Separate head hardware avoids the printed overhang at the cost of another part inside the source passage.
